From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-maintainer <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:19:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stats: never clear local achievement data without Cloud
 Redirect

Hooks_NetPacket_UserStats answers ClientGetUserStats with an empty stats
payload and eresult OK whenever the app has any depot registered in the
Lua config. CloudRedirect was supposed to overlay the real achievements
afterwards, but its GetAchievements() returns 0 as soon as the host is
inactive (cloud_redirect.dll absent or [cloud].enabled = false).

The client takes that empty-but-OK answer at face value and rewrites
appcache\\stats\\UserGameStats_<steamid>_<appid>.bin into the 38-byte
skeleton, which is exactly the "achievements vanish after re-importing a
game" report: dropping the lua and re-adding it rebuilds the depot set,
the hook fires again, and the local progress is gone.

Bail out early instead, so the untouched response reaches the client and
Steam keeps the on-disk stats.
---
 src/Hook/Hooks_NetPacket.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Hook/Hooks_NetPacket.cpp b/src/Hook/Hooks_NetPacket.cpp
--- a/src/Hook/Hooks_NetPacket.cpp
+++ b/src/Hook/Hooks_NetPacket.cpp
@@ -368,6 +395,15 @@ namespace Hooks_NetPacket_UserStats {
             LOG_ACHIEVEMENT_DEBUG("ClientGetUserStats response: no modification needed");
             return false;
         }
+        // Without CloudRedirect there is nobody to supply real achievements,
+        // and an empty-but-OK reply makes the client overwrite the local
+        // UserGameStats_<steamid>_<appid>.bin with its 38-byte skeleton.
+        // Leave the packet alone so Steam keeps whatever is on disk.
+        if (!CloudRedirectHost::IsActive()) {
+            LOG_ACHIEVEMENT_DEBUG("ClientGetUserStats response: CloudRedirect inactive, leave stats untouched (app {})",
+                                  resp.game_id());
+            return false;
+        }
+
         resp.clear_stats();
         resp.clear_achievement_blocks();
         resp.set_eresult(1);  // k_EResultOK
